1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:05,000
Select the released seed-42 checkpoint for inference.

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:08,600
Check that the full protein feature cache is present.

3
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:12,800
Check the Docker image used for this evaluation.

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:18,900
Run the published evaluation script on the mixed test set.

5
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:25,100
The script loads the checkpoint and protein features. No training is needed.

6
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:34,900
Of 1,679 FASTA records, two contain unsupported bases.
The remaining 1,677 match the benchmark test IDs.

7
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:11,080
1,677 records scored. AUROC 0.9217, accuracy 0.8748.

8
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:17,200
Run the published evaluation script on the species holdout.

9
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:25,200
Use the same checkpoint and the same decision threshold of 0.5.

10
00:01:54,800 --> 00:02:00,680
1,164 records scored. AUROC 0.8845, accuracy 0.8308.

11
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:06,800
Run the published evaluation script on the protein-family holdout.

12
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:14,800
This set tests generalization to held-out protein families.

13
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:49,580
817 records scored. AUROC 0.8815, accuracy 0.7809.

14
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:55,200
Compare this run with the seed-42 entries in the paper’s Source Data.

15
00:02:55,400 --> 00:03:03,100
AUROC and accuracy match the reference to four decimal places on all three sets.
